_TO_LOCAL_STATUS.get(status_raw)` — a hardcoded reverse literal separate from the rebar-status label path","inbound_translate.py:133 `mapping = getattr(cfg_mod, 'jira_to_local_status', {})` consumed by apply_inbound_events.py:164,336","Plan item 4 scopes inbound recovery to 'parsing the rebar-status:<local> suffix against the effective reverse vocabulary'; the workflow-status reverse read is not named as a threading site","Plan item 1 adds `effective_jira_to_local` but only item 4 (label parse) names a consumer"],"finding":"The inbound WORKFLOW-STATUS reverse lookups (inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields line 306 `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS.get(status_raw)`, and inbound_translate._jira_status_to_local reading built-in `jira_to_local_status`, consumed by apply_inbound_events.py:164,336) are not clearly threaded to the new `effective_jira_to_local`. Plan item 1 introduces `effective_jira_to_local(project_key, root)` (a per-project config-driven reverse map), but item 4 and the Scope entries for inbound describe inbound recovery ONLY as 'parsing the rebar-status:<local> label'. It is ambiguous whether a config-remapped status (e.g. default.status_map remapping a status to a different Jira name) round-trips inbound at the plain workflow-status level, or whether those two literals stay pinned to the built-in.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f868bc9f899395525","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach items 1 & 4; Scope entries for inbound_fields.py / inbound_translate.py / apply_inbound_events.py","norm_id":"n23542190b92284bc","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A [mapping.default] status_map override changes a Jira workflow status name; inbound translation of that Jira status back to local still uses the built-in reverse map and mis-maps or drops it"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserte