the fetcher and would trip a spurious unmapped-status alert.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f41c94081354a0927","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (files) — fetcher.py absent","norm_id":"ne3bbe8dcdd6e9cda","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project adds a Jira status via [mapping.projects.<KEY>] reverse override; the fetcher's known-set still reflects only the built-in and files a spurious 'has no reconciler mapping' bridge alert every pass"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the reverse-map inventory for `effective_jira_to_local` via find_referencing_symbols on `jira_to_local_status`/`_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS`/`_jira_status_to_local` (plus a string grep), and enumerate every consumer that must adopt the effective reverse map — including inbound_translate._jira_status_to_local, inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields, apply_inbound_events.py callers, and fetcher.py._known_jira_statuses (currently absent from Scope).","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1222,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: `effective_jira_to_local(project_key, root=None)` ... `reverse = canonical preimage plus config's reverse overrides`","Plan step 4: inbound recover `by parsing the rebar-status:<local> suffix against the effective reverse vocabulary` — scoped to the label helper only","Scope names inbound_translate/inbound_differ/apply_inbound_events/inbound_fields but only for the label parse-helper (`use the shared parse helper (retire the duplicated _REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL)`)","inbound_translate.py:133 `_jira_status_to_local` reads `getattr(cfg_mod, 'jira_to_local_status', {})` — not the effective reverse map","inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields reads `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS.get(status_raw)` (the plan's own named test oracle) — never switched","fetcher.py:180-182 `_known_jira_statuses()` reads `config.jira_to_local_status` keys and is not in Scope"],"finding":"The plan introduces `effective_jira_to_local` (step 1) as the config-driven reverse resolution seam but does not enumerate the production workflow-status reverse-map consumers as sites that switch to it. The Scope lists inbound files (`inbound_translate.py`, `inbound_differ.py`, `apply_inbound_events.py`, `inbound_fields.py`) only for the `rebar-status:` label parse-helper migration, leaving the actual Jira-status→local reverse lookups reading the built-in `config.jira_to_local_status`/`_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS` unchanged. `fetcher.py`, a reverse-vocabulary consumer, is absent from Scope entirely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc2e3cf682d35cbf6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 (`effective_jira_to_local`) and step 4 (inbound recovery); Scope (files) inbound entries","norm_id":"n9809c38456b00595","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["inbound_translate._jira_status_to_local (inbound_translate.py:107-133): a config reverse override in [mapping] never reaches Jira→local status translation; imported/synced status lands at the built-in reverse target, diverging from the effective map.","inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields: the plan's named test oracle keeps using the built-in _JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS, so test_status_collapse_roundtrip's inbound leg may pass against the wrong seam.","apply_inbound_events.py:164 and :336 (_apply_inbound_update / create) invoke _jira_status_to_local — unpatched, freshly imported issues land at the built-in local status regardless of config.","fetcher.py _known_jira_statuses / _flag_unmapped_statuses: unmapped-status detection stays keyed on the built-in config.jira_to_local_status, so a config that maps a new Jira status is still flagged 'no reconciler mapping'."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add fetcher.py to Scope and state explicitly which reverse-map consumers switch to effective_jira_to_local vs. which stay on the built-in; if only the label helper consumes the new reverse seam, say so and justify why _jira_status_to_local / _map_jira_to_local_fields / _known_jira_statuses remain on the built-in map.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the stamp rule's behaviour when `status_map[local]` has no entry in the effective reverse map (use `.get(...)` semantics — treat a missing reverse entry as 'no canonical preimage' → stamp, or as 'no target' → skip) so a config overlay adding a forward target absent from the reverse map cannot raise KeyError.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3888,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Built-in map covers all targets (value_maps.py:78 forward, config.py:64 reverse), so the rule is safe today, but a config overlay adding a forward target absent from the reverse map has no total-coverage guarantee under 'reverse = canonical preimage plus config's reverse overrides'","Approach step 4 says a DRIFTED status has no target and no label, but is silent on a MAPPED-but-reverse-absent target"],"finding":"The generalised stamp rule `effective_jira_to_local[status_map[local]] != local` uses direct subscript indexing on the reverse map, but the plan's reverse map ('canonical preimage plus config's reverse overrides') is not guaranteed to contain every forward target. A config overlay that maps a local status to a Jira name with no reverse entry (e.g. `status_map: {foo: \"Backlog\"}` with no `Backlog` reverse) will raise KeyError in the label diff — a crash on exactly the config-driven path this ticket introduces.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffc6fe0e401a002c6","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 — 'stamp `rebar-status:<local>` iff `effective_jira_to_local[status_map[local]] != local`'","norm_id":"nddffdabbbcb84160","priority":0.2112,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator adds `[mapping.default] status_map = {triage = \"Backlog\"}` without a corresponding reverse entry; the outbound label diff evaluates the stamp rule for `triage` and raises KeyError"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Define the rule as: stamp iff `effective_jira_to_local.get(status_map[local]) != local` (a `None`/absent reverse entry ⇒ no canonical preimage claims `local`, so annotate).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a documentation deliverable (AGENTS.md or a config reference) describing the `[mapping]` status_map contract: SKIP vs absent-drift vs collapse round-trip via `rebar-status:` labels.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan defines novel config semantics: 'SKIP = intentional drop; a status ABSENT is the drift case' and 'any non-injective collapse must round-trip via rebar-status:'","Scope file list contains no docs/AGENTS.md/design-doc entry"],"findin